To set up BGP for automatic path switching in your 6PE IPv6 setup, configure the add-paths capability for labeled-unicast routes. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "YOUR_GROUP_NAME"
        add-paths
            label-ipv6 send 2 receive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `YOUR_GROUP_NAME` with your BGP peer group name. The `send 2` parameter advertises up to 2 alternate paths per prefix, while `receive` enables acceptance of multiple paths from peers. 

For neighbor-specific configuration instead of group-level:
```
configure router bgp
    neighbor 2001:db8::1
        add-paths
            label-ipv6 send 2 receive
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Adjust the `send` limit (2-16) based on your network redundancy requirements. This allows immediate failover to pre-exchanged backup paths upon link failure without new BGP negotiations.
