To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to advertise up to 8 different next-hops for the same IPv4 route and allow the neighbor to accept multiple routes per prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "your_group_name"
        neighbor "neighbor_IP_address"
            family ipv4
            add-paths ipv4 send 8
            add-paths receive
            third-party-nexthop
exit all
```

### Key details:
- **`add-paths ipv4 send 8`**: Enables advertising up to 8 different next-hops for the same IPv4 prefix.
- **`add-paths receive`**: Allows the router to accept multiple paths per prefix from the neighbor.
- **`third-party-nexthop`**: Preserves the original next-hop when advertising to EBGP peers in the same subnet (prevents unintended next-hop modification).
- **`family ipv4`**: Ensures IPv4 address-family is active for the neighbor.

Replace `"your_group_name"` and `"neighbor_IP_address"` with your actual BGP group and neighbor IP. This configuration maintains standard BGP path selection while enabling multi-path sharing.
