To configure BGP for handling both MPLS-labeled IPv6 and EVPN Layer 2 in the same peering setup on a Nokia 7750 SR, use the following CLI commands. This enables both address families under the same BGP group while ensuring multicast VPN IPv6 add-paths capabilities are properly set:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "YOUR_GROUP_NAME"
        family ipv6 labeled-unicast
        family evpn
        add-paths
            mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive
        exit
    exit
```

**Key details:**
- `family ipv6 labeled-unicast`: Activates MPLS-labeled IPv6 traffic handling
- `family evpn`: Enables EVPN Layer 2 services
- `mvpn-ipv6 send 8 receive`: 
  - Negotiates send/receive capabilities for multicast VPN IPv6 routes
  - `send 8` advertises up to 8 paths per prefix
  - `receive` accepts multiple paths from peers
  - Adjust the `8` to match your path scale requirements

Replace `YOUR_GROUP_NAME` with your BGP peer group name. This configuration ensures both IPv6 MPLS and EVPN Layer 2 coexist in the same BGP session without conflicts.
