To handle routes containing your own AS in the AS path silently without disrupting the BGP session, configure an import policy to reject these routes:

```cli
/configure router policy-options
    begin
    as-path-expression "local-as" expression ".* <your-as-number> .*"
    policy-statement "drop-local-as" entry 10
        from as-path "local-as"
        action reject
    exit
    commit
exit
```

Apply this policy to the BGP neighbor or group:
```cli
/configure router bgp 
    group <neighbor-group-name> 
        import "drop-local-as"
    exit
exit
```

Replace:
- `<your-as-number>` with your actual AS (e.g., `64500`)
- `<neighbor-group-name>` with your BGP peer group name

This configuration:
1. Matches any route containing your AS in the AS path
2. Silently discards these routes (`reject` action)
3. Maintains the BGP session unaffected
4. Prevents accidental route readvertisement
