To achieve near-instantaneous BGP updates for IPv6 multicast VPN routes during multicast group changes, enable BGP add-paths for multicast VPN IPv6 routes with the following configuration:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> add-paths
    mvpn-ipv6 send <send-limit> receive
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your BGP group and neighbor IP address. Set `<send-limit>` to the maximum number of paths you want to advertise per prefix (e.g., `2` or `3`). This configuration:

1. Enables transmission of multiple paths per multicast VPN IPv6 prefix (`send <send-limit>`)
2. Allows receiving multiple paths from peers (`receive`)
3. Bypasses the default single-path limitation that causes update delays

For global application to all neighbors within BGP, use:
```
configure router bgp add-paths
    mvpn-ipv6 send <send-limit> receive
exit
```

This configuration accelerates route propagation during join/leave events by advertising multiple paths simultaneously, eliminating the wait for best-path reelection.
