            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter
                            sr-ospf
                        exit
                    exit
                    family ipv6
                        resolution-filter
                            sr-ospf
                        exit
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- The `sr-ospf` command ensures BGP prefers SR tunnels from the OSPF instance with the lowest preference value (or lowest instance ID if preferences are equal).  
- Apply this to both IPv4 (`ipv4`) and IPv6 (`ipv6`) families under `shortcut-tunn` (for regular BGP routes) and `labeled-routes` (for labeled BGP routes).  
- Remove any higher-priority tunnel types (e.g., `ldp`, `rsvp`) from the `resolution-filter` if they shouldn't be considered.  

This configuration forces BGP to prioritize SR tunnels advertised by the least-preferred OSPF instance when resolving next-hops.
